A||||10||pontiacs4me||shaved door handles project||||1||
Z||000000||pontiacs4me||04-09-2001||10:14 PM||||Ok, heres another of my bad ideas.  A friend of mine got his Acura integra repossed and before the bank came to get it he pulled the shaved door handle kit out of it, and he sold it to me for 20 bucks.  I shaved the handles on my firebird and it cost me 275 for that one.  I figured may as well shave the handles on the fiero.  But what to do about the moulding that runs right along with the handle?  Im thinking of finding a piece of quarter panel moulding and shaving it into where the handle goes.  Then filling the area where the ressesed part is.  Do you guys, (and gals) think this will look good?  Has anybody done this yet?  Im going to take some more pics of the fiero tomorrow and edit it out on photo shop.  Ill post some pics of that project tommorow.  let me know what you think of that Idea.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fyerstarter||04-09-2001||11:17 PM||||What exactly is in this "shaved door handle kit"? Is this just the solonoids to pop the doors or are you talking about something to aid in the body work? <P>I think it would look ok if you shaved just the door handles, but better all the molding altogether. Don't get any ideas though because I am going to be the first one to do it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||04-10-2001||12:11 AM||||Pontiacs4me, have you seen this thread?:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006394.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006394.html</A> <P>Just some help with the visualization, but don't get too carried away!  Warning, these images may lead to further bad ideas!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||04-10-2001||03:41 AM||||Nope, I never saw that thread.  None of those were about what I was thinking.  I thought about shaving the moulding, but there would be some major problems there. One you would have to fabricate a body line where the existing moulding is.  that would be very difficult to do, and to get perfectly straight.  and two, none of the panels would be servicable if need be, without major destruction.  What I plan to do is shave the handle area, and make it like one piece of solid moulding from the front of the door to the back.  <BR>Fyerstarter, I have 2 solenoids and a relay box that works on a radio frequency tuned to a remote control with 2 buttons on it.  when you push a button, it sends the signal to the solenoid to activate, and it yanks down on the door latch and your door pops open.  Check out this picture of my firebird with shaved handles. <A HREF="http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/bird3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/bird3.jpg</A>  this is for real also, not computer enhanced.  BTW, the spoiler piece is missing because this was the day after I painted the car and I had to spray under it, because of some body work I had to do to the area.  <BR>Im going to take that pic of Haze's silver car and edit it in photoshop, and Ill post it here and on the other thread, to show you all what Im talking about.||||reg||1
Z||000004||pontiacs4me||04-10-2001||04:08 AM||||Here it is.  <A HREF="http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/hazefiero1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://home.kscable.com/ccheney/ryanpict/hazefiero1.jpg</A>  <BR>after seeing it now, ive decided to go ahead with it, along with shaving the pontiac arrowheads on the window pilars, and the rear bumper reflector lights.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wolfhound||04-10-2001||07:37 AM||||It would be possible to fabricate a piece of full length door mold using the original molding to make a mold.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroSEt||04-10-2001||09:23 AM||||I'm working on the smoothed trim area on my fastback convertion right as we speak. I dont have a digital camera so I try to get some pic's on here when finished. I'm also fiberglassing the sail scoop's in there to, and loosing the tail pipe area too( my exhaust comes straight out and down of the flowmaster). also adding side marker light's just below the original place front and back(off of a 1980Old's Omega). It is real hard to get it smooth and level. I've been working on the passenger side for a few day's now!!  I also shaved the side mirror's too. I can't wait until I'm through this summer!!!!   I'll keep everybody posted... ANY SUGGESTION'S WELCOME!!!!!!  Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka... 1FieroGTRacingInc.<BR>       Tyler,Texas<BR>Fiero_87GT@Yahoo.com||||reg||6
Z||000007||shiloh187||04-10-2001||02:08 PM||||how hard are these molding pieces to make or get made?  I was planning on doing this door conversion also but wasnt sure how to do to door molding.<P>shaving the mirrors? i think i will pass on that one...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>shiloh||||reg||1
Z||000008||Taijiguy||04-10-2001||03:52 PM||||I started to eliminate my door handles and install a latch kit, but I worried a bit about the reliability factor. I can see them on a car that has no windows, but if you ever had trouble with the system, you'd be screwed unless you had a back-up plan. What would you do? Bust out the sunroof? How else could you get in... <BR>~Taiji <IMG SRC="http://members.core.com/~taijiguy/eye2.gif">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Taijiguy (edited 04-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||pontiacs4me||04-10-2001||09:43 PM||||Ive had shaved door handles on my firebird for a year now, I only have problems in the winter.  they get real cold, and freeze up.  So I made a tool, kind of like a slimjim, out of a bent pushrod, and I keep it in my trunk.  If my solenoids freeze up, I can pop the trunk and get it out and slide it down between the weatherstrip and the window glass onto the top of the latch.  then I just push down and the door opens.  You dont have to worry about door locks, because with no handles, how is a theif going to get inside.  Just dont let anybody see you, if you ever have to break into it.  BTW, I only had to break into my car about 5 times last winter.||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroSEt||04-11-2001||02:43 PM||||Yep...  I'm shaving off the side mirror's too, only because I have the 4 foot *Wink* mirror. Using the Wink mirror you don't even need the side mirror's at all...  I might add some side mirror's later up on the pillar.  Anyone else use the *wink* style mirror??  <P>------------------<BR>aka... 1FieroGTRacingInc.<BR>       Tyler,Texas<BR>Fiero_87GT@Yahoo.com||||reg||1
